      "rev_n_1_68c30d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_68c30d_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_68c30d",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the angle between the target and the origin. Use this angle to determine the point on the spiral where the avatar should detach. This approach leverages the symmetry and properties of the Archimedean spiral.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403880.193778
      },
      "rev_n_2_f91641_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_f91641_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_f91641",
        "thought_text": "Simulate the movement of the avatar along the spiral and check for the intersection condition. Use a binary search to find the precise angle where detaching results in hitting the target without intersecting the spiral. This method ensures accuracy but may be computationally intensive.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403880.193983
      },
      "rev_n_3_86f6da_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_86f6da_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_86f6da",
        "thought_text": "Derive a formula to calculate the exact point on the spiral where the avatar should detach based on the target's position. This involves solving equations that relate the spiral's geometry to the target's location. This approach aims for a direct solution with minimal computational overhead.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403880.193999
      },
      "rev_n_4_9266b6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_9266b6_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_9266b6",
        "thought_text": "Consider using numerical methods to iteratively find the correct detachment point. This involves checking potential points on the spiral and verifying if the path to the target intersects the spiral.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6647362711622859718",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403943.568133
      },
      "rev_n_5_86e6e0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_86e6e0_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_86e6e0",
        "thought_text": "Explore the use of vector projections to determine the correct angle of detachment. By projecting the target vector onto the tangent of the spiral, we can find the optimal detachment point.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6647362711622859718",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403943.568161
      },
      "rev_n_6_a28500_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_a28500_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_a28500",
        "thought_text": "Implement a binary search on the angle phi to find the exact point of detachment. This approach ensures precision and efficiently narrows down the correct angle by comparing distances.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6647362711622859718",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403943.5681732
      },
      "rev_n_7_c794a9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_c794a9_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_c794a9",
        "thought_text": "Refine the binary search bounds to dynamically adjust based on the target's position relative to the spiral. This could reduce the number of iterations and improve performance.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-9216533161268181507",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403984.618494
